.. dropdown:: Technical details
    :class-container: dk-default-value

    This option is only relevant when using the :attr:`font_context` setting. The specified font
    family will be requested from the active font context, but it may not exist, or multiple fonts
    may share the same family name.

    The value must be a family name (`string`) available in the selected font context—for example,
    a system font in a ``system://`` context, or a custom font registered through
    :class:`kivy.core.text.FontContextManager`.
    If set to `None`, font selection is determined by the :attr:`font_name` attribute.

    .. tip::
        When referencing a custom font file via :attr:`font_name`, this attribute should remain `None`.
        The family name is automatically managed in that case.

    .. note::
        This feature requires the Pango text provider.

